abstract: >-
  ChemRob DJ predicts pharmacological activity and safety liabilities from
  chemical structure across 21 classification heads and 57 individual targets,
  trained on 255,804 molecules curated from ChEMBL and CO-ADD. It is released
  alongside a controlled measurement of how much evaluation design, rather than
  the model, determines reported performance: holding data, features and
  hyperparameters fixed, the split protocol moves macro AUPRC by 0.2388 while
  the molecular representation moves it by 0.0655, the estimator by 0.0503 and
  the labelling scheme by 0.0094. Every evaluation artifact behind those numbers
  is versioned in artifacts/.
